<!--
TUTORIAL — Diátaxis quadrant: learning-oriented.

The reader is new and wants a first success. Rules:

- ONE path. No branching, no "if you prefer X". Alternatives are how-tos.
- Every command is pasteable and every output is real. Never invent
  numbers or paths; run it and copy what printed.
- The reader makes no decisions. You choose for them and say so.
- Use "you" and the imperative. "Run this", not "one can run".
- Explain only what is needed to proceed. Link the rest.
- End with what they saw and where to go next.

Frontmatter: `time` is an honest estimate. `needs` is what they must have
before starting, in one clause. Delete either if not applicable.
-->

